#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1363 expect=violation domain=DM
#note "FLIPPED by the M2-P9 ruling (option (b) / M2-D29, Fix #307) exactly as finding SD1363-F1 pre-authored it: rename, expect=violation, count 1, row=1 ARMCD=A. Row 1 carries the fifth ARMNULRS term 'SCREENING NOT COMPLETED', added to SDTM CT codelist C142179 in the 2025-09-26 package, nearly three years after the PMDA v6.0 row was written. Such a subject was never assigned to treatment, so by the sheet's own reasoning ARMCD/ARM must be null; the shipped two-name membership list left it silent. Row 2 is a conformant control ('SCREEN FAILURE', ARMCD/ARM empty) that keeps the fixture from passing vacuously. Mirror: fda/FDA-SD1363/FDA-SD1363-invalid_screening_not_completed-DM.cdt."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 ARMCD=A
dataset DM label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col ARMCD   type=Char label="Planned Arm Code"
col ARM     type=Char label="Description of Planned Arm"
col ARMNRS  type=Char label="Reason Arm and/or Actual Arm is Null"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1015 | A | Arm A | SCREENING NOT COMPLETED
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1023 |   |       | SCREEN FAILURE
